course: dictionary
lesson: 3041
title: Words for things we wear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An earring is a noun, a naming word for a thing. It is a piece of jewellery worn on the ear, usually through a small hole in the earlobe. You can say a pair of earrings, or wear earrings.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Take off rings, earrings and necklaces before sport, because they can catch and tear skin.» Rings, earrings and necklaces are all things you wear, and the earring is the one worn on the ear.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «He sends money and presents: a tablet, gold earrings, sweets.» Gold earrings fits, because earrings are jewellery, and a tablet and sweets are not worn on the ear.
fact: An earring is a piece of jewellery worn on the ear.
fact: Most earrings go through a small hole in the earlobe.
fact: Clip-on earrings do not need a hole; they clip onto the ear.
fact: «Girl with a Pearl Earring» is a famous painting by Johannes Vermeer, painted around 1665 in the Netherlands.
fact: Nobody knows who the girl in the painting was; a later novel and film invented a story about her.
exercise: «Take off rings, earrings and necklaces before sport.» What is an earring? | A piece of clothing worn on the feet | *A piece of jewellery worn on the ear | A kind of sports ball | A tool for cutting paper
exercise: Which word means more than one earring? | ear | *earrings | earring | earlobe
exercise: When was «Girl with a Pearl Earring» painted? | 1889 | *Around 1665 | 1508 | 1937
test: Where is an earring usually worn? | *On the ear | On the knee | On the hand | On the foot
test: In «Take off rings, earrings and necklaces before sport, because they can catch and tear skin», why must they come off? | *They can catch and tear skin | They are too heavy for shoes | To look smart | They get lost in the bag
exam: Which word in «Rings, earrings and necklaces come off before sport» names something worn on the ear? | necklaces | rings | before | *earrings
